WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.872 --> 00:00:17.914
Once more, Swallow felt proud after his good deed.

2
00:00:19.295 --> 00:00:21.296
And once more, he was ready to go.

3
00:00:22.877 --> 00:00:24.779
He searched the docks for the ship to Egypt.

4
00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:28.261
He didn't need to follow it—he knew the way.

5
00:00:30.182 --> 00:00:33.404
But traveling alone seemed lonely and tiring.

6
00:00:36.106 --> 00:00:38.807
Swallow spotted the ship and started to dive down.

7
00:00:40.947 --> 00:00:43.428
But a hawk was circling overhead.

8
00:00:45.169 --> 00:00:47.770
It was the same one that Swallow had seen yesterday.

9
00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:51.252
"If I land, it will catch me!"

10
00:00:51.272 --> 00:00:56.534
As Swallow shot away, he saw someone familiar below.

11
00:00:58.495 --> 00:01:01.856
The girl who was selling eggs now stood outside a building.

12
00:01:03.048 --> 00:01:04.249
She was with other children.

13
00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:07.752
Swallow perched in a tree to watch.

14
00:01:09.333 --> 00:01:11.255
The girl showed the jewel to the others.

15
00:01:11.275 --> 00:01:13.877
"We'll never go hungry again!"

16
00:01:13.897 --> 00:01:18.001
The children cheered.

17
00:01:20.002 --> 00:01:21.483
Swallow's heart swelled.

18
00:01:22.464 --> 00:01:24.846
"I must tell Prince about this before leaving!"

19
00:01:28.549 --> 00:01:31.512
But when Swallow reached the statue, he saw a crowd.

20
00:01:33.232 --> 00:01:36.335
Some people looked sad, others angry.

21
00:01:36.355 --> 00:01:41.579
"Our beautiful statue is ruined!"

22
00:01:42.159 --> 00:01:42.960
a woman cried.

23
00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:46.763
"Two of its jewels are gone!"

24
00:01:48.665 --> 00:01:50.426
"We must find the thief!"

25
00:01:50.947 --> 00:01:51.767
a man shouted.

26
00:01:51.787 --> 00:01:55.550
"Our Happy Prince is turning ugly."

27
00:01:55.570 --> 00:02:00.414
"Ugly?" Swallow scowled.

28
00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:02.136
"That's not nice!

29
00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:07.001
And his beauty shines—in all his generous deeds.

30
00:02:08.002 --> 00:02:09.482
You people should thank him!"

31
00:02:13.924 --> 00:02:16.025
Only the statue heard Swallow's words.

32
00:02:16.045 --> 00:02:18.506
"It's okay, Swallow.

33
00:02:19.366 --> 00:02:20.427
I don't need thanks.

34
00:02:21.387 --> 00:02:22.808
It's the right thing to do.

35
00:02:24.108 --> 00:02:26.349
Tell me, why have you returned?"

36
00:02:26.369 --> 00:02:33.052
"I came to tell you how happy the orphans are," Swallow said.

37
00:02:34.904 --> 00:02:37.425
"That's wonderful," said the statue.

38
00:02:37.445 --> 00:02:41.107
"My heart feels a bit lighter now.

39
00:02:42.787 --> 00:02:44.488
But you'd better leave for Egypt.

40
00:02:45.709 --> 00:02:46.969
A storm is coming."

41
00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:49.110
Swallow looked up.

42
00:02:50.511 --> 00:02:53.292
The sky was gray, and it started to rain.

43
00:02:53.312 --> 00:02:57.994
"I was planning to fly to Egypt with a ship.

44
00:02:59.034 --> 00:03:00.575
But it won't sail in this weather.

45
00:03:01.815 --> 00:03:03.216
I'll stay one more night."

46
00:03:07.552 --> 00:03:10.374
He curled up in the warm spot between the statue's feet.

47
00:03:11.454 --> 00:03:12.435
But he couldn't sleep.

48
00:03:13.896 --> 00:03:14.916
He had an idea.

49
00:03:18.038 --> 00:03:22.200
Later, after the storm, Swallow flew to the statue's shoulder.

50
00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:25.202
"You have one jewel left.

51
00:03:26.362 --> 00:03:28.944
Before I go, let me take it to someone in need."

52
00:03:28.964 --> 00:03:32.245
"Yes," said the statue.

53
00:03:32.265 --> 00:03:36.748
"Take it to the three children who live under the bridge."

54
00:03:42.156 --> 00:03:45.378
Swallow plucked the sapphire and flew toward the bridge.

55
00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:50.481
He passed many people who needed help.

56
00:03:50.501 --> 00:03:55.244
"I wish I could help everyone," he thought.

57
00:03:57.925 --> 00:04:00.667
Swallow found the three children huddled under the bridge.

58
00:04:01.767 --> 00:04:05.089
They were thin and cold, with no blankets or coats.

59
00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:09.712
Swoosh! He dropped the jewel in their pot.

60
00:04:11.976 --> 00:04:13.918
As he flew off, he heard them shout.

61
00:04:13.938 --> 00:04:17.120
"Was that a bird?"

62
00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:18.341
the boy cried.

63
00:04:18.361 --> 00:04:22.644
"Yes, and it gave us a jewel!"

64
00:04:23.105 --> 00:04:23.985
his sister said.

65
00:04:24.006 --> 00:04:27.768
"Now we can buy clothing!"

66
00:04:27.788 --> 00:04:29.910
"And food!"

67
00:04:30.551 --> 00:04:31.992
the littlest one shouted.
